# Wazuh Lab Credentials Template

> [!CAUTION]
> NEVER commit actual production or personal passwords to Git. Copy this file to `secrets/credentials.md` (which is git-ignored) for local notes.

## Default Lab Credentials (Single-Node Docker Stack)

| Service | Component | URL / Port | Username | Default Password | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Wazuh Dashboard** | Web UI | `https://localhost:443` | `admin` | `SecretPassword` | Single-node default admin account |
| **Wazuh Indexer** | REST API | `https://localhost:9200` | `admin` | `SecretPassword` | OpenSearch compatible indexer |
| **Wazuh API** | Manager API | `https://localhost:55000` | `wazuh-wui` | `MyS3cr37P450r.*-` | Used by dashboard & automation scripts |
| **Indexer Internal**| Kibana server | Internal | `kibanaserver` | `kibanaserver` | Dashboard internal communication |
| **Agent Auth** | Registration | `manager_ip:1515` | N/A | None / Enrolled | Authd agent registration service |

## Custom Environment Overrides
To change passwords before initial launch:
1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`
2. Update the passwords in `.env` and `config/wazuh_indexer/internal_users.yml`
3. Generate new certificates if hostnames change
